std::bind with two or more placeholders.  _Bind::operator()'s defaulted
_Result parameter expands the call's own _Args pack (tuple<_Args...>,
[temp.param]/14 + [temp.variadic]/5); the pack's deduced ELEMENTS must be
recorded before the default is evaluated, or the default saw tuple<int> for a
two-argument call and _Safe_tuple_element_t<1, ...> (the second placeholder)
failed, leaving the call operator with no viable overload.
Tagged libstdcxx12: with libstdc++ 11 (the 22.04 CI runners' host gcc) this
test does not pass yet -- see .kiro/decltype_tuple_apply_findings.md, round
157 (std::bind/tuple with three or more elements: the recursive __and_ of
libstdc++ 11 mis-binds its pack from the fifth argument on; <locale>
has_facet dereferences).
